keel-lnpp-19.0 (10) keel; urgency=high

  * A new build with keel-overlay-coraza 0.1.5 and keel-web 0.4.4 from the
    Keel archive. keel-overlay-coraza 0.1.4 inspected a request body that
    had no Content-Type header. One request with no login could make a
    worker use more than 1 GB of memory. No other file of this repository
    changed.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (9) keel; urgency=medium

  * lnpp.yaml named gunicorn of the check page as a process. Monit requires
    each process of a manifest to be active, but the socket unit starts
    gunicorn at the first request only. So 2 to 4 minutes after each boot
    where nobody had asked /keel-check/, Monit started it and keel sent the
    critical alert "keel-lnpp-check fails its check" (CT 9364 on BR1, a
    node of an Odoo pair with the socket and the application of lnpp put
    back, 2026-11-10; Monit log: status failed at 04:21:52 and 04:23:53,
    then the alert and the restart). The commissioning runs did not see it, because
    the contract asks the page of each node in the first minutes.
  * The check page is no process of the manifest now. systemd holds the
    socket and starts gunicorn at a request, as before; the contract
    requires keel-lnpp-check.socket and asks the page.
  * A layer built on lnpp inherits the processes of lnpp.yaml and cannot
    remove one. Odoo removes the check page, so each Odoo node had this
    process with nothing that could start it: Monit sent the same alert and
    stopped the watch (release A3, the two Odoo pairs).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:40:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (8) keel; urgency=medium

  * The commissioning test of handbook decision 0075 (a container made from
    the template on BR1 and BR2, as an operator makes it) found these
    defects, 2026-11-06:
  * firstboot.d/36pgsqlverify stopped with "fatal: no DB_PASS" when no
    password was declared: on the headless first boot, and under keel-init,
    where 35pgsqlpass asked the password on the console and the inithooks
    conf is empty. A headless boot now leaves the question to keel-init
    (console_deferred of inithooks); at a console the hook reads the
    catalogue as postgres by peer and requires a password there. The copy
    of keel-postgresql has the same change.
  * keel/instance.example.yaml named app.options.db_user, which no manifest
    of the chain declares, and named no appliance, so keel never checked it
    against the manifests. The example now names the appliance,
    installation.mode and the nine overlays of Core and Web, and no option;
    the pair example declares overlays.syncthing.
  * tests/commission.yaml, the commissioning contract, and the CI job
    "commission / contract" that checks it.
  * The contract asks port 80 of the loopback, as keel-web 0.4.0 serves it
    (handbook decision 0079): http://127.0.0.1/ and /keel-check/ 200,
    /keel-health 204.
  * The cloud part of the contract takes the shape of the reference
    contract of .github: hotkeys in the menus, the wait screen, the VIP
    holder by "carried here: yes", a row written on the primary and read on
    the standby, the Syncthing folder types, a writable server after a
    promote, and the check page of the replica says that its server is
    read-only.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000

keel-lnpp-19.0 (7) keel; urgency=medium

  * Stable 1 refresh of 2026-10-30 (decision 0073). The image is built again
    from the pool stable-1 (apt#88) with the Debian security fixes of
    2026-10-30: nginx (DSA-6575), bind9 (DSA-6576), php8.4 (DSA-6574),
    imagemagick (DSA-6593), libheif (DSA-6583), brotli (DSA-6582),
    ca-certificates (DSA-6572) and tzdata 2026f. It carries keel 0.23.67: a
    MariaDB primary does not accept a write before its replica connects
    (keel#242), and the manifest adds state.replicate of a base to that of
    the application (keel#246). It also carries inithooks 2.3.6+keel35 and
    confconsole 2.2.3+keel19.

